WEBVTT

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:04.870
And then?

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.630
My brother's...

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.130
I saw Naotaka Natsume's grave.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.420
Naotaka-san's?

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.150
What does this mean?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.590
But you've received letters from him.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.410
That's right. I even met him.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.260
I've seen him, too.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.910
Then what was that grave?

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.340
"Naotaka Natsume"

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:31.810
What? My brother?

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.010
Hello?

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.160
Get out of there immediately.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.160
Is it really you?

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.180
Just run.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.090
What are you...

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:53.160
Misao?

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.310
Come on.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.360
What is that, a Picasso-mask?

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.660
Let's get out of here, Tomoharu.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:22.860
Tomo!

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.240
R-right!

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.500
<i>Asura Cryin' 2</i>

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.380
"The Truth Dedicated to You"

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.170
What's going on?

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:17.720
Mahiwa!

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:27.650
Go, Vivian!

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:56.930
Looks like we lost her.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:58.610
What's going on?

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.460
I'm not sure either.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.780
We're being chased by a mystery Picasso-mask person.

00:04:03.190 --> 00:04:04.420
Picasso-mask?

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.390
Mahiwa, can't we fly any higher?

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.920
That's impossible. We're already way over capacity!

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:10.710
Here comes the Picasso-mask!

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.640
W-who is that scary looking person?

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.880
Vivian, let's get out of here!

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.020
Mahiwa, fly straight ahead!

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.460
Get off the road!

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:39.670
Take this!

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.050
What's up with those reflexes?

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.270
That's got to hurt.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.330
I'll take care of her.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:04.410
No way!

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.670
Immune to magic? Could it be...?

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.050
Go up!

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:11.630
Vivian!

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:18.390
We did it!

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.420
Nice one, koala!

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.150
What? No way...

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.190
Gotcha!

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.500
Tomo, call Kurogane!

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.620
I can't here!

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.230
Mahiwa-kun, we've got to go faster!

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.020
Get to the factory above the cliff!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:02.720
She's gone.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:03.890
Where'd she go?

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:05.390
Natsume-kun!

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.370
That phoenix...

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:23.400
You!

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.360
My name is Hiwako Torishima.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.710
I doubt our association will be very long...

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:32.800
...but it's a pleasure to make your acquaintance, Tomoharu Natsume-sama.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.350
We're surrounded.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.380
Yes.

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:47.490
What's going on?

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.160
Why did you attack me?

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:50.690
What are you trying to do?

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:58.240
Looks like they're not here to chat.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:00.790
Tomo.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.910
Asura Machina?

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:36.340
Hagane...

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.220
Misao?

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:41.120
Inside, everyone! Quickly!

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:45.850
Wait, Misao!

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:07.740
Where are we?

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.350
We're near the Meiotei.

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:13.140
Huh? What's going on?

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.790
Teleportation?

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:18.020
Do you know, Sao-chan?

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:20.990
What?

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.600
Oh, come on.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.250
What just happened?

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.450
Oh, that...

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.780
What?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:44.960
Oh, the Meiotei blew up.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.350
According to local residents...

00:08:56.350 --> 00:09:00.760
...a number of explosions have occurred at this mansion in the past...

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:04.810
...and the area was widely regarded as a danger zone.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.580
"A danger zone!"

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:10.070
You don't care at all, do you, President Rikka?

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.570
Of course I don't.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:15.950
The police are searching for the building's resident, a high school student...

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:19.530
...thinking he may have some information regarding the incident.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.000
Isn't that you, Tomo?

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.880
You're a wanted man!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.140
The real culprit must be Hiwako or Picasso-mask.

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:29.340
They knew the Meiotei was the only place Tomoharu would go.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:33.920
The Science Club's armory and my equipment were in the basement, too.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:34.570
What?

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:36.770
You were hiding dangerous stuff down there?

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.620
Tomoharu, did you do anything to make them hate you?

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.620
Huh? Why?

00:09:43.910 --> 00:09:47.140
Well, they were clearly out for your blood.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:47.990
What?

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:50.080
I don't remember doing anything.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:54.570
This was probably just a declaration of war.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.010
This could turn into something big.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:57.920
But why?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:09:59.830
Well?

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:02.590
Why did you call me out here at this hour?

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.790
I wanted to formally request the services of the Second Student Council for a particular job.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:07.560
A job?

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:12.730
I need you to protect Nia-chan and our club president while he's at school.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:14.780
Huh? Shuri-san...

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.400
There's nothing we can do...

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:20.010
...but we can't afford to have Nia-chan caught in the middle of any more fighting.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:21.810
Fine.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:24.980
Our services won't be cheap, though.

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.620
That won't be a problem.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.940
Nia-chan will earn us more than enough.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.620
The luck eater.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:33.140
I see.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:36.380
With this girl's ability to manipulate the odds...

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:38.550
...the money would come pouring in.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.690
What a twisted smile.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:42.980
Are you really okay with this?

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.420
Did you hear what she said?

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:46.100
It can't be helped.

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:49.890
I don't want to owe them any debts...

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:53.650
...and I don't want to get in your way any more, either.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:57.350
Looks like we have a deal.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:58.820
Okay.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:00.670
In that case, Tomoharu Natsume.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:01.260
Yes?

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.750
You'll be sleeping in the church.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.490
What?

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.370
Why?

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:09.540
The farther you are from us, the safer we'll be.

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:12.390
I always get the job done.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.000
Right.

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:21.140
What's wrong, Tomo?

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:28.340
I was just thinking about how the Meiotei was blown up.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:30.720
Yeah.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:34.210
This is a pretty big deal for me.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.680
The police are after me.

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.030
Where am I supposed to live?

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:40.650
Natsume-kun.

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.170
Takatsuki-san?

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:46.170
I brought you a blanket.

00:11:46.580 --> 00:11:48.170
I thought it might get cold at night.

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:51.080
Thanks.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:56.540
Do you have a minute to talk?

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:58.010
Yeah, sure.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:11:59.620
Oh, uh...

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:02.000
...do you want to sit with me?

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:17.100
This almost feels nostalgic.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:17.630
Huh?

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:23.120
The first time you saved me was in a chapel.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.000
But that was just...

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:31.940
You were only caught because you were trying to save me...

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:34.730
...and Misao was the one making Kurogane move.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:42.390
I'm still useless.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:45.420
I always have to be saved by you or Misao.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:01.110
You're so high maintenance.

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:06.690
I sent Shuri Kurosaki to protect you and gave you Kurogane.

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:10.180
I even set up the Science Club at Rakurowa High School, just in case.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:15.000
But somehow, you still end up in the thick of things.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:17.610
What's going on, Tomoharu?

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:18.320
Is something...

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:20.200
Naotaka!

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:21.170
What?

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:22.050
Naotaka?

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:23.750
W-what do you mean?

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.400
What do we mean?

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:26.840
That's Naotaka-san.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:27.930
Isn't he your brother?

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.330
No...

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:32.830
...I've never seen this man before.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:35.300
Who are you?

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:37.120
Where is my brother?

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:39.500
The real Naotaka Natsume...

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.230
...died studying abroad.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:43.490
Y-you're lying!

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.930
I hate to break it to you, but it's true.

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:48.810
Naotaka Natsume died...

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:51.280
...so I passed myself off as him.

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.300
It happened to serve my purposes.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:55.770
I'll ask you one more time.

00:13:56.150 --> 00:13:57.950
Who are you?

00:13:57.950 --> 00:14:00.500
Are you allied with Picasso-mask and Hiwako Torishima?

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:05.440
I'm the Tomoharu Natsume from the first world.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.960
In other words, I'm you.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:11.580
The first world?

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:14.510
Yes. That dying world.

00:14:15.890 --> 00:14:18.270
The first world I was living in...

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:21.180
...failed at its black hole experiment...

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:22.740
...and is approaching its end.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:25.000
The world is vanishing...

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:26.730
Exactly.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.700
I used the Asura Machina Hagane's power...

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:34.670
...to cross the boundaries between worlds and come to the past...

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.020
...so I could save my world.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:41.330
I'll do it.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:43.620
Then that was...

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:48.500
You were the one I saw in those memories at the Rakuroa ruins?

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:49.760
I see.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.910
Echoes of memory.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.050
That's right.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:54.640
Natsume-kun.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:00.960
You were opening a trunk.

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:04.390
You said you used the powers of an Asura Machina, right?

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.160
What are they?

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:08.390
What are the Asura Machina?

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:12.410
They're probes for traveling between our connected worlds.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:13.650
Probes?

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:14.380
Yes.

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:17.930
We made a deal with demons to make the Asura Machina...

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:21.810
...the last hope of a species abandoned by God.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:23.100
Why?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.220
Why is Misao trapped inside of one?

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:27.310
I'm sorry.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.210
I'm running out of time.

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:36.560
He's vanishing.

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:41.050
You failed to overwrite his existence, didn't you?

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:43.960
So you know, Nia?

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.310
It was in my sister's research.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:48.810
What are you talking about?

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:50.890
People coming from another world...

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:54.450
...attempt to overwrite their other self.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.680
In simpler terms...

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.620
...the newcomer takes over the old self.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:01.290
But those that fail to overwrite...

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:05.520
...are seen as demonic by the world...

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:06.290
...and rejected.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.960
This is the result.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.630
If Naotaka-san is actually the first world's Tomoharu...

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:14.630
...then this isn't right.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.600
I couldn't overwrite your existence...

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:20.390
...because when I came here from the first world...

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:22.270
...you were already dead.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:23.620
Dead?

00:16:23.850 --> 00:16:24.670
Yeah.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.140
Isn't that right, Misao?

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:28.320
What?

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.050
Misao, you...

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:32.610
...did you already know all of this?

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:34.280
I had forgotten...

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:36.280
...but I remembered everything...

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:38.480
...when I saw that Asura Machina.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:40.630
The first world's Tomo.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:42.390
I get it.

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:45.880
That explains why you seemed so familiar.

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:51.790
What do you mean?

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.370
Tell me!

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.690
I don't want to be the only one in the dark any more!

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.370
Tomo...

00:16:58.780 --> 00:16:59.750
Sure.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:01.190
I'll tell you all about it.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.770
That day four years ago, when Misao became a burial doll.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:07.560
Everything about it was irregular.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:17.580
This can't be.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:18.550
He's dead.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.510
Did I fail?

00:17:35.410 --> 00:17:36.410
Tomo...

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:39.850
No. Tomoharu Natsume is dead.

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:43.310
No...

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.830
Black wings?

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:55.740
A demon?

00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:58.500
Is that what you are?

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:01.700
Please...

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:03.080
...save Tomoharu.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:05.580
I don't care what happens to me. Just save Tomo.

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:08.280
You're a demon, right?

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:13.010
I'll give you my life, my soul, anything. Please.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:14.040
Why?

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:16.980
If Tomo dies...

00:18:17.590 --> 00:18:19.940
...there won't be anything for me to do.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:28.260
Misao...

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:58.250
You have me, Tomo.

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:03.210
Using Misao's soul and Hagane's power...

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:06.710
...I brought back your dying body back and overwrote it.

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:12.730
Misao chose to become a burial doll to save me?

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:14.080
Yes.

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:18.520
Why?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.280
Why would you do that?

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:24.160
How...

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:26.860
How do I free her?

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:34.000
I've made arrangements for you.

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:37.320
Stay hidden in the location indicated by that map.

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:44.010
You and Kurogane are spares in case I fail at my mission.

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:45.310
Spares?

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.450
Try not to die, okay?

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:55.180
Space manipulation powers.

00:19:58.700 --> 00:19:59.580
Takatsuki!

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:12.650
She's having a paroxysm! She can't control her magic!

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:13.740
Takatsuki!

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:15.360
Hang in there, Takatsuki!

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:16.770
What should we do?

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:21.470
Ritsu-chan gave me this...

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:28.370
Takatsuki!

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:38.860
Looks like the medicine is working.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.880
I had no idea it would advance this quickly.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:47.820
She's been using using her powers recklessly without a contractor.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:49.370
It's to be expected.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:53.220
She fought knowing this would happen to her.

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.690
She's prepared for the consequences.

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:56.830
Why...

00:20:57.100 --> 00:20:58.420
Natsume-kun...

00:20:58.890 --> 00:20:59.800
Takatsuki...

00:21:01.360 --> 00:21:02.180
I...

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:03.910
I'm sorry.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:05.000
I'm sorry.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.760
It's okay, Takatsuki.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.670
It's no big deal.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:10.170
I'm sorry.

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:13.080
I'm fine, so...

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:16.280
...until the very end, I'll...

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:18.280
What "end?"

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:30.530
You've really gotten yourselves into trouble this time.

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.440
What do you want, Haruna?

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:34.700
Reckless use of a daughter...

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:37.750
...unsanctioned combat in the city and property damage.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.460
Tomoharu Natsume...

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:43.860
...and members of the Rakurowa High School Science Club...

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:46.300
...are to be detained.

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:22.210
The tearing world.

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:23.360
Let go of your treasures.

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.530
Sticking to your throat.

00:23:24.530 --> 00:23:25.650
Scraps of junk.

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:27.180
If you gather them up...

00:23:27.180 --> 00:23:29.060
...you'll find the tearing world.

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:31.350
Quiet your voice and use your heart.

00:23:31.990 --> 00:23:34.980
"Moment of Annihilation, Darkness of Extinction"
